From 0b29a74b591a911f6055e76e6f2b60d1799217fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Mete=20Fatih=20C=C4=B1r=C4=B1t?= <mfc@autoware.org>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 17:16:11 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(gpu_backend): share the uploaded map between copies
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A copy of the NDT object uploaded the map again in its first align().
In Autoware, the map update thread copies the NDT object and swaps the
copy in, so this upload ran in the scan callback while it held the NDT
lock, once per map update.

Uploaded maps never change, because setTarget() makes new device
buffers. So copies now share the buffers of the original through a
shared_ptr and need no upload. A copy also sizes its scratch buffers
when it is made, so its first align() allocates nothing.

Signed-off-by: Mete Fatih Cırıt <mfc@autoware.org>
